# Copy to services/.env (gitignored; chmod 600): docker compose reads it from the
# project directory (services/) to fill in ${...} in docker-compose.yml. It holds
# host paths and, optionally, the two Slack webhooks of Grafana's GPU health
# alerts, which only the grafana service receives. The file itself is not passed
# into any container. See README.md, 6.1.
# The values below are the live layout on cvglsuppvm. Before using them
# elsewhere, create the directories for uid 1000 (see README.md, section 4).

# Prometheus TSDB directory, mounted at /prometheus. Owner uid 1000 (Prometheus
# runs as 1000:1000), on a local disk. REQUIRED, with no default on purpose:
# without it every `docker compose` command run in services/ stops with an error,
# so that Prometheus is never started on the old NFS directory
# /srv/nfs/var/prometheus, which is kept unchanged only as a rollback copy.
PROMETHEUS_TSDB_DIR=/home/cvgladmin/.local/share/cluster-setup-monitoring/prometheus

# Directory of the Determined token file ("token"), mounted at
# /run/determined-metrics: read-write in watchdog, read-only in prometheus.
# Owner uid 1000, mode 0700 (sudo install -d -m 0700 -o 1000 -g 1000 <dir>).
# Optional: if unset or empty, ./prometheus/secrets (gitignored) is used.
DET_METRICS_SECRETS_DIR=/home/cvgladmin/.local/share/cluster-setup-monitoring/secrets

# Slack incoming webhooks of Grafana's GPU health alerts (README.md, 7.4), passed
# to the grafana service only. Optional: unset or empty, Grafana uses a dead local
# address, starts normally and delivers no GPU alert. Copy the values from
# determined-watchdog/.env with the command in README.md, 7.4 (critical =
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL, application XIDs = SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL_DEBUG); never commit them.
# SLACK_GPU_CRITICAL_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/<secret>
# SLACK_GPU_APP_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/<secret>
